Federal agencies offered AI-powered reporting, analytics, workflow automation, and decision-support tools at steep discounts

WASHINGTON — Today, the U.S. General Services Administration (GSA) announced a new OneGov offering with CORAS, a provider of secure agentic AI, to accelerate AI adoption across federal agencies and equip them to automate manual, repetitive tasks that tie up staff and delay mission goals.

GSA is building on the momentum of OneGov by extending agreements, expanding access to AI services, and laying the groundwork for scalable AI infrastructure across the federal government in accordance with President Trump’s White House AI Action Plan [PDF].

> This partnership with CORAS expands the range of AI-enabled capabilities available to agencies as they evaluate solutions that support mission and operational requirements,

said FAS Acting Commissioner Laura Stanton.

> Through OneGov, GSA is providing agencies access to commercial technologies through standardized acquisition pathways and innovative pricing structures.

Through this offer, eligible customers can access discounted pricing for GARY, the agentic AI orchestrator at the core of the CORAS FedRAMP High, IL 5/6 platform. Gary turns plain-language requests into decision-ready work products by directing a digital workforce of specialized agents, with human reviewers in the loop at every step.

Additionally, the platform’s “App Factory” allows agencies to build mission-specific applications in a matter of days without any custom development, far surpassing the current six-to-twelve-month timeline for traditional app development.

> CORAS is pleased to participate in the OneGov initiative and support agencies evaluating AI-enabled approaches to operational workflows and decision-support activities,

said Dan Naselius, president and chief technology officer of CORAS.

> Gary runs a governed digital workforce that takes the manual analysis, reporting, and paperwork off people’s desks and executes it under human-authored rules, with a person approving every result and a full audit trail behind it.

The offer includes two primary product families:

GARY Insight (80% discount): Includes agentic reporting and ETL capabilities, advanced analytics, dashboard generation, and access to the CORAS agent catalog.

GARY Execute (40% discount): Includes agentic workflows, orchestration, enterprise decision-support capabilities, and AI configuration support.

Discounted pricing is available until September 30, 2027, through GSA’s Multiple Award Schedule under the OneGov Strategy. Product details, ordering guidance, and points of contact for all OneGov limited-time offers are available on the OneGov webpage.

###

About GSA: GSA provides centralized procurement and shared services for the federal government, managing approximately 360 million rentable square feet, overseeing over $126 billion in products and services via federal contracts, and delivering technology services to millions of people across dozens of federal agencies. GSA’s mission is to deliver exceptional customer experience and value in real estate, acquisition, and technology. To address nearly $50 billion in delinquent maintenance, GSA is leading a coalition of every cabinet agency and many federal leaders urgently advocating for full Federal Buildings Fund access and raising the prospectus threshold from $3.96 million to $75 million. For more information, visit GSA.gov and follow @USGSA.

